      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{2}:=8R_{2}$ on $N?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{2}:=8R_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $8.$\n\nMultiplying the $2$nd row by $8$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=8R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 8\\cdot 0 & 8\\cdot (-6) & 8\\cdot (-6) & 8\\cdot 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -48 & -48 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
