      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 6 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 8 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -8 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_{1}$ on $M?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_{1}$ means that we need to multiply the first row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $1$st row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 6 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 8 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -8 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-9) & -\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\ 9 & 8 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 8 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -8 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
